  "summary": "Confirmed the three-vector blank-screen analysis by reading both smartPollBoard() (index.html:410-464) and smartPollFeatures() (client.html:528-614). Both functions share identical structural flaws: (1) the fetch chain does `r.text()` without checking `r.ok`, so non-200 error bodies get parsed as HTML, find zero `.stage-section` elements, and trigger `container.innerHTML = html` — replacing the board with error text; (2) even on valid 200 responses, if the server returns HTML with zero stage-sections (e.g., during a transient reconnection window), the `newSections.length !== curSections.length` branch fires and blanks the container; (3) `_lastBoardHTML`/`_lastFeaturesHTML` is assigned before any DOM diffing, so an error or empty response poisons the cache and the next valid response will always diff as changed, creating a flash. The fix for each polling function is: add `if (!r.ok) return Promise.reject()` in the first `.then()`, add `if (newSections.length === 0) return` before any DOM mutation, and move the `_lastBoardHTML = html` / `_lastFeaturesHTML = html` assignment to after the DOM update succeeds. The `.catch(function() {})` already silently swallows errors, so the reject path is safe. These are three surgical, coordinated changes per function — no architectural refactor needed."
